NAME
       vgremove - delete a volume group

SYNOPSIS
       vgremove [-f] [-y] VG...

DESCRIPTION
       vgremove deletes a volume group. If the group still contains logical
       volumes, vgremove asks before removing each of them (and their data);
       -f removes them without asking. Unmount their file systems, deactivate
       swap on them and remove their /etc/fstab lines first. The PVs stay
       PVs; clear them with pvremove if the disks are needed for something
       else.

OPTIONS
       -f, --force
              Remove the logical volumes without asking.

       -y, --yes
              Answer yes to questions.

EXAMPLES
           umount /mnt/data
           lvremove /dev/vgdata/lvdata
           vgremove vgdata
           pvremove /dev/vdb1

SEE ALSO
       vgcreate(8), lvremove(8), pvremove(8)
